    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "5ffca2ed91bb2e010813c008",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/da85e010de6ab170974f99acaf5d8b09?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FMR-6.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/da85e010de6ab170974f99acaf5d8b09?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FMR-6.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/da85e010de6ab170974f99acaf5d8b09?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FMR-6.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/da85e010de6ab170974f99acaf5d8b09?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FMR-6.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Michael Ritter",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=5ffca2ed91bb2e010813c008",
      "timeZone": "America/Denver"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "I have a few questions from things I’ve run into today while writing integration tests to cover use cases: ",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "content": [
           {
            "content": [
             {
              "text": "in ",
              "type": "text"
             },
             {
              "attrs": {
               "url": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-3321"
              },
              "type": "inlineCard"
             },
             {
              "text": " the webac filter  was updated so that authenticated users could start transactions. Is this something we want to keep? Or should we have the default acl restrict to authorized only.",
              "type": "text"
             }
            ],
            "type": "paragraph"
           }
          ],
          "type": "listItem"
         },
         {
          "content": [
           {
            "content": [
             {
              "text": "I was working on an integration test to show a case with an acl which allows fedoraUsers to write on ",
              "type": "text"
             },
             {
              "marks": [
               {
                "type": "code"
               }
              ],
              "text": "rest/fcr:tx",
              "type": "text"
             },
             {
              "text": " and was realized that the changes I made shouldn’t have impacted the root acl. I rolledback my commits and retried using the default acl and receive 403s for PUT/POST/DELETE on ",
              "type": "text"
             },
             {
              "marks": [
               {
                "type": "code"
               }
              ],
              "text": "rest/fcr:tx/${uuid}",
              "type": "text"
             },
             {
              "text": " so I guess at this point I’m wondering if there’s anything that needs to be done other than the question above. ",
              "type": "text"
             }
            ],
            "type": "paragraph"
           }
          ],
          "type": "listItem"
         }
        ],
        "type": "bulletList"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
