      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/da85e010de6ab170974f99acaf5d8b09?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FMR-6.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/da85e010de6ab170974f99acaf5d8b09?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FMR-6.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/da85e010de6ab170974f99acaf5d8b09?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FMR-6.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/da85e010de6ab170974f99acaf5d8b09?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FMR-6.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Michael Ritter",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=5ffca2ed91bb2e010813c008",
      "timeZone": "America/Denver"
     },
     "body": "<p>I have a few questions from things I’ve run into today while writing integration tests to cover use cases: </p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>in <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-3321\" title=\"smart-link\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-3321</a> the webac filter  was updated so that authenticated users could start transactions. Is this something we want to keep? Or should we have the default acl restrict to authorized only.</li>\n\t<li>I was working on an integration test to show a case with an acl which allows fedoraUsers to write on <tt>rest/fcr:tx</tt> and was realized that the changes I made shouldn’t have impacted the root acl. I rolledback my commits and retried using the default acl and receive 403s for PUT/POST/DELETE on {{rest/fcr:tx/$\n{uuid}\n<p>}} so I guess at this point I’m wondering if there’s anything that needs to be done other than the question above.</p></li>\n</ul>\n",
     "created": "27/Oct/22 5:10 PM",
     "id": "22742",
     "jsdPublic": true,
